  "headnotes": [
    {
      "la": "…ta est in superiori editione, et Bernardi in Cantica Sermonibus subjuncta tanquam genuinus ejus fetus, quem Guillelmus Sancti Theoderici abbas designaverit in lib.* I *de ejus Vita cap. 12, his verbis",
      "en": "…nd appended to Bernard's Sermons on the Song of Songs as a genuine offspring of his, which William, abbot of Saint-Thierry, is said to have designated in Book I of his Life, chapter 12, in these words",
      "column": "407",
      "chunk": 0
    },
    {
      "la": "…m homine studioso et pio concinnatum. Quam vero designat Guillelmus, ipsa esse videtur quae sub ejus nomine edita est in tomo IV Bibliothecae Cisterciensis: ubi attendenda sunt Praefationis haec verba",
      "en": "…tudious and pious man. But the one which William designates seems to be that which was published under his name in Volume IV of the Cistercian Library: where these words of the Preface are to be noted",
      "column": "407",
      "chunk": 0
    },
    {
      "la": "Quae verba recte praemissis ex Vita Bernardi conveniunt, cum ait Guillelmus se a Bernardo expositionem in Cantica petiisse",
      "en": "Which words rightly agree with the passage set forth above from the Life of Bernard, when William says that he had asked of Bernard an exposition on the Song of Songs",
      "column": "407",
      "chunk": 0
    },
    {
      "la": "…, quia nolo ut alteram de istis eligas, sed utramque teneas, contemplativam scilicet vitam et activam; o pulchra inter mulieres, si vis nosse me, noli ignorare te. Hoc est responsum Delphici Apollinis",
      "en": "…ne of these, but that thou hold both, namely the contemplative life and the active; O fairest among women, if thou wouldst know me, be not ignorant of thyself. This is the answer of the Delphic Apollo",
      "column": "425b",
      "chunk": 7
    }
  ],
